# D12 (QA-REPORT-11): NOTHING under baselines/ was ever tracked (`git ls-files
# baselines/` = empty) — it is pure runtime output. The old per-file patterns
# (*.png, index.json, runs.db, *.db) leaked any new file type the runtime
# grows into `git status --short` (prod: `?? baselines/`), breaking the
# 207e329 law that an empty status is a machine-checkable receipt.
# Ignore the whole dir.
/baselines/
